model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway.accountConnections {
    metadata {
      constraint "Grouped sign-in removal follows the identity row menu and its Manage apps item before selecting a binding; the fixture preserves existing refusal and sibling checks. Account row actions show safe listed identity and local drafts while details load. Saving and deleting require the account read's permission and the authoritative host mutation; listed data never grants write authority. Untouched fields follow fresh metadata, typed fields survive transient read failures, retry and loss of write permission without permitting a write; read-only dialogs focus Close rather than a disabled-field hint. Denial or removal clears protected forms, and removing one saved sign-in preserves its siblings. Accounts, app Accounts and setup actions share this behavior. Sharing keeps its independent early reads, and loaded identities retain the title derived from reported account health."
    }
  }
}
